<title>UK: SOCCER-BECK FREE TO PLAY SAY MIDDLESBROUGH.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BECK FREE TO PLAY SAY MIDDLESBROUGH.</headline>
<dateline>MIDDLESBROUGH, England 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Middlesbrough insisted on Thursday that Danish international striker Mikkel Beck will be eligible to play for them even though former club Fortuna Cologne are demanding compensation for his move.</p>
<p>Keith Lamb, chief executive of the English premier league side, stressed that Beck will be able to play &quot;at all levels&quot; while the issue was being resolved.</p>
</text>
